<title>BELGIUM: Belgian construction sector sales fell in 1996.</title>
<headline>Belgian construction sector sales fell in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-03-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgian construction sector sales fell to 900 billion Belgian francs in 1996 from 940 billion in 1995, the National Chamber for the Construction Industry said on Monday.</p>
<p>Sales accounted for eight percent of gross domestic product in 1996, it added. While sales in the civil engineering and commercial construction sector fell, the housing sector saw an increase by 17 percent. It gave no further details.</p>
<p>Employment in the sector fell to 173,000 from 179,485 in 1995. Bankruptcies rose to an all-time high of 7,100 in 1996 from 2,081.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
